1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:01,883
[playful music playing]

2
00:00:02,592 --> 00:00:03,927
[Ayame] Hey, sissy.

3
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:06,930
It seems like Chii
doesn't even want a boyfriend.

4
00:00:07,014 --> 00:00:09,433
She said she's too busy with basketball.

5
00:00:09,516 --> 00:00:12,728
What? Give me a break!
She's a girl in high school!

6
00:00:12,811 --> 00:00:15,063
This is the age
when people fall in love with each other!

7
00:00:15,147 --> 00:00:17,816
I've been on high alert
for the past few days.

8
00:00:17,899 --> 00:00:21,319
And there's basically no end to the guys
who seem interested in her.

9
00:00:23,655 --> 00:00:27,117
If I were her, I'd go down the line
and chat each one of them up.

10
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,453
Yeah, but you're not an ordinary person.

11
00:00:29,536 --> 00:00:31,955
I wonder if there's someone
she's got her eye on.

12
00:00:34,291 --> 00:00:37,669
Sissy, you do know you always get quiet
when my guesses are right.

13
00:00:37,753 --> 00:00:39,838
{\an8}- [groans softly]
- Who is it? Who is it?

14
00:00:39,921 --> 00:00:41,089
{\an8}Do I know this someone?

15
00:00:41,173 --> 00:00:44,801
{\an8}Now! I need his name, age, birthday,
and his emergency contact!

16
00:00:44,885 --> 00:00:46,970
{\an8}You expect me to know all that?

17
00:00:47,054 --> 00:00:50,932
{\an8}[Ayame] If Chii's interested in him,
then this must be some awesome guy!

18
00:00:51,808 --> 00:00:53,018
Could it be...

19
00:00:53,101 --> 00:00:56,021
[gasps] They got to know each other
while practicing in the gym?

20
00:00:56,104 --> 00:00:57,105
Who could say...

21
00:00:57,189 --> 00:00:59,399
{\an8}Who is it? Who is it? Who is it?

22
00:00:59,483 --> 00:01:01,401
{\an8}I need you to spill the tea!

23
00:01:01,485 --> 00:01:04,237
{\an8}- Please, please, please, tell me.
- <i>This is not good.</i>

24
00:01:04,321 --> 00:01:07,199
{\an8}<i>If she finds out about him,
she'll definitely meddle.</i>

25
00:01:07,282 --> 00:01:09,493
{\an8}<i>-Maybe I should lie to her.</i>
- Please, sissy.

26
00:01:10,285 --> 00:01:12,245
{\an8}[Chinatsu] He's totally awesome!

27
00:01:12,329 --> 00:01:14,247
He's my favorite player.

28
00:01:14,331 --> 00:01:16,291
Spill the tea!

29
00:01:16,374 --> 00:01:18,668
- C'mon, sissy!
- [sighs]

30
00:01:18,752 --> 00:01:19,753
Are you listening?

31
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,049
The person Chii likes
is this tall, older, handsome guy.

32
00:01:24,132 --> 00:01:26,384
He's a bit wild, and good at basketball.

33
00:01:26,468 --> 00:01:28,762
He lives overseas in another country.

34
00:01:28,845 --> 00:01:30,263
[gasps]

35
00:01:31,097 --> 00:01:33,266
That sounds like a great match!

36
00:01:34,142 --> 00:01:36,812
Anyone less than that
wouldn't be good enough for her.

37
00:01:36,895 --> 00:01:38,647
[Karen] <i>It's a lie.
But this is still better</i>

38
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:40,732
<i>than her finding out the truth, right?</i>

39
00:01:40,816 --> 00:01:42,400
[playful music ends]

40
00:01:43,110 --> 00:01:44,778
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

41
00:01:44,861 --> 00:01:46,071
{\an8}[coach] Kazuma Matsuoka,

42
00:01:46,154 --> 00:01:49,157
{\an8}our second-year who was studying
in the U.S. is back with us.

43
00:01:49,241 --> 00:01:50,534
Thanks. It's good to be back.

44
00:01:50,617 --> 00:01:52,661
- [Ayame gasps]
- [all] Welcome back!

45
00:01:52,744 --> 00:01:55,122
[Ayame] <i>A tall handsome guy
who just came back from overseas</i>

46
00:01:55,205 --> 00:01:56,665
<i>and is good at basketball?</i>

47
00:01:59,584 --> 00:02:00,961
<i>That's the guy!</i>

48
00:02:03,839 --> 00:02:05,841
[opening theme song playing]

49
00:02:30,198 --> 00:02:33,618
BLUE BOX

50
00:03:33,637 --> 00:03:35,680
{\an8}EPISODE 22
INOTA!

51
00:03:35,764 --> 00:03:38,433
{\an8}[Ayame] <i>A tall handsome guy
who just came back from overseas</i>

52
00:03:38,516 --> 00:03:40,185
<i>and is good at basketball.</i>

53
00:03:40,268 --> 00:03:43,188
<i>I didn't think that kind of superhuman
actually existed,</i>

54
00:03:43,271 --> 00:03:46,233
<i>but that guy right there
is a perfect match for her.</i>

55
00:03:46,316 --> 00:03:48,360
<i>Chii! I'm rooting for you!</i>

56
00:03:48,443 --> 00:03:50,153
- [Taiki] Manager.
- [Ayame groans]

57
00:03:50,237 --> 00:03:51,363
[upbeat music playing]

58
00:03:51,446 --> 00:03:53,823
I do have a name after all,
and it's hella cute.

59
00:03:53,907 --> 00:03:55,200
Ayame? Ring a bell?

60
00:03:55,283 --> 00:03:58,328
Okay, then, Ayame,
you forgot to fill this part out.

61
00:03:58,411 --> 00:04:01,498
What? But I double-checked it
and everything.

62
00:04:01,581 --> 00:04:04,834
What the...
Was he always in basketball club?

63
00:04:05,627 --> 00:04:07,963
He studied abroad for a year,
which so explains

64
00:04:08,046 --> 00:04:10,715
why he's not only handsome,
but also worldly!

65
00:04:10,799 --> 00:04:12,968
And rumor is
he's really good at basketball.

66
00:04:13,843 --> 00:04:15,470
Isn't he the coolest?

67
00:04:17,305 --> 00:04:20,350
{\an8}Though, if I'm being honest,
Yusa is more my type!

68
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:22,394
{\an8}Haven't you only seen the guy one time?

69
00:04:22,477 --> 00:04:23,603
[footsteps]

70
00:04:23,687 --> 00:04:25,605
- [Taiki] Hina.
- [Hina] Hm?

71
00:04:25,689 --> 00:04:26,898
What's up?

72
00:04:26,982 --> 00:04:28,066
So, did you hear?

73
00:04:28,149 --> 00:04:30,610
The other day during practice,
Uchida from Volleyball Club--

74
00:04:30,694 --> 00:04:33,113
Yeah, I've got the deets
on that one already.

75
00:04:33,196 --> 00:04:35,615
[Ayame] <i>It's the cute girl
from the Rhythmic Gymnastics Club.</i>

76
00:04:36,241 --> 00:04:38,368
{\an8}[laughs] Old news!

77
00:04:39,035 --> 00:04:40,120
[Ayame] Hm.

78
00:04:40,704 --> 00:04:41,955
[Hina] Huh?

79
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:47,377
[Ayame] <i>Well, well, well.</i>

80
00:04:48,336 --> 00:04:50,255
<i>Something is going on there.</i>

81
00:04:51,464 --> 00:04:54,884
{\an8}BURNABLE

82
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,221
So gross.

83
00:04:58,305 --> 00:05:01,141
There's no way I can make
taking out the trash look cute.

84
00:05:01,224 --> 00:05:02,726
[footsteps approaching]

85
00:05:03,727 --> 00:05:04,811
[gasps softly]

86
00:05:06,354 --> 00:05:09,524
- Hi there again.
- Huh? Oh, yeah, hello.

87
00:05:15,822 --> 00:05:17,032
[Ayame] Excuse me, but...

88
00:05:17,115 --> 00:05:18,199
Yes?

89
00:05:18,283 --> 00:05:20,660
I'm asking you because
I'm manager of Badminton Club,

90
00:05:20,744 --> 00:05:23,788
and this is probably
gonna come back to me somehow...

91
00:05:23,872 --> 00:05:26,791
Tell me, do you have feelings for Inota?

92
00:05:26,875 --> 00:05:28,043
{\an8}What?

93
00:05:28,126 --> 00:05:30,170
- Yes! I could sense it!
- [groans]

94
00:05:30,253 --> 00:05:33,298
You were making a girly face back there,
so I was suspicious.

95
00:05:33,381 --> 00:05:34,924
I so was not.

96
00:05:35,008 --> 00:05:37,552
Inota's not to be underestimated, then!

97
00:05:37,635 --> 00:05:40,555
Especially if a cute girl like you
is interested in him.

98
00:05:40,638 --> 00:05:43,641
And don't worry,
he's not the kinda guy I go for.

99
00:05:44,893 --> 00:05:47,771
You can lock him down,
Rhythmic Gymnastics.

100
00:05:47,854 --> 00:05:49,564
Um, what was your name?

101
00:05:49,647 --> 00:05:50,690
Hina Chono.

102
00:05:50,774 --> 00:05:53,735
He's the kind of guy
who just needs a little push.

103
00:05:53,818 --> 00:05:57,072
But once Inota knows how you feel,
he'll wanna date you for sure.

104
00:05:57,155 --> 00:06:00,700
{\an8}Oh, he already knows how I feel about him.

105
00:06:00,784 --> 00:06:03,161
[Ayame] What? You confessed to him?

106
00:06:03,703 --> 00:06:04,704
[Hina] Yep.

107
00:06:04,788 --> 00:06:07,957
But I told him
I didn't need a response right away.

108
00:06:08,041 --> 00:06:09,167
To be honest with you,

109
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:12,754
I had a feeling that he had
only been looking at me as a friend.

110
00:06:12,837 --> 00:06:13,838
[Ayame] Hm.

111
00:06:13,922 --> 00:06:17,092
I didn't think it would help
keeping my feelings to myself.

112
00:06:17,926 --> 00:06:21,137
And I wanted him to see me
as a possible girlfriend.

113
00:06:21,221 --> 00:06:22,097
Huh?

114
00:06:22,764 --> 00:06:25,016
So, he still hasn't given you an answer?

115
00:06:25,558 --> 00:06:26,476
Uh-huh.

116
00:06:26,559 --> 00:06:30,021
Do you think it's because you said
you weren't in a hurry to get one?

117
00:06:30,563 --> 00:06:31,481
Yeah, maybe.

118
00:06:31,564 --> 00:06:33,108
{\an8}[grunts angrily]

119
00:06:33,191 --> 00:06:37,278
What's with him?
Confessing to someone takes guts, and yet,

120
00:06:37,362 --> 00:06:39,364
he's making you do all the work?

121
00:06:39,948 --> 00:06:43,076
Isn't he just taking advantage
of the fact that you like him?

122
00:06:43,159 --> 00:06:44,494
[Hina sighs]

123
00:06:44,577 --> 00:06:47,747
Chono, listen, you can't let him
be free-range anymore.

124
00:06:47,831 --> 00:06:50,291
You've gotta grab him
by the neck and capture him.

125
00:06:52,127 --> 00:06:54,129
Aren't you exhausted the way things are?

126
00:06:54,712 --> 00:06:55,630
Not really.

127
00:06:56,381 --> 00:06:59,259
{\an8}It's actually fun having a crush on Taiki.

128
00:06:59,342 --> 00:07:00,343
[gasps]

129
00:07:01,094 --> 00:07:04,013
- That's adorable.
- [groans softly]

130
00:07:05,181 --> 00:07:07,308
[Ayame] <i>Does he not know
that there aren't many girls</i>

131
00:07:07,392 --> 00:07:10,019
<i>who will care about him
as much as she does?</i>

132
00:07:11,438 --> 00:07:12,522
[gasps]

133
00:07:13,148 --> 00:07:14,524
Okay. Leave it to me.

134
00:07:15,442 --> 00:07:18,528
Your love is gonna be reciprocated.
I'm gonna help you.

135
00:07:18,611 --> 00:07:19,779
Wait, really?

136
00:07:20,447 --> 00:07:21,781
<i>I'm Ayame Moriya.</i>

137
00:07:21,865 --> 00:07:24,909
<i>An ally to girls out there
giving it their all.</i>

138
00:07:24,993 --> 00:07:26,619
<i>Just you wait, Inota!</i>

139
00:07:37,755 --> 00:07:38,673
[gasps softly]

140
00:07:45,889 --> 00:07:48,558
[whimsical music playing]

141
00:07:49,309 --> 00:07:50,351
[sighs]

142
00:07:52,896 --> 00:07:54,314
- Inota!
- [exclaims]

143
00:07:54,397 --> 00:07:55,565
Yes?

144
00:07:55,648 --> 00:07:58,318
Chinatsu, why are you
calling me that now, too?

145
00:07:58,401 --> 00:08:00,695
I just thought it was a good nickname.

146
00:08:00,778 --> 00:08:03,448
Don't call me that.
I think it's kinda embarrassing.

147
00:08:03,531 --> 00:08:04,449
Oh, really?

148
00:08:04,532 --> 00:08:07,368
Well, you wouldn't like it
if I called you "Chii," would you?

149
00:08:07,452 --> 00:08:08,328
INOMATA

150
00:08:08,411 --> 00:08:10,079
- Actually...
- Huh?

151
00:08:10,163 --> 00:08:11,331
I wouldn't mind...

152
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:14,459
{\an8}if you were to call me Chii.

153
00:08:14,542 --> 00:08:15,710
[gasps softly]

154
00:08:15,793 --> 00:08:16,961
Ha. Not.

155
00:08:17,545 --> 00:08:18,963
<i>What?</i>

156
00:08:19,672 --> 00:08:21,716
- [door slides]
- [Chinatsu] I'm home.

157
00:08:22,592 --> 00:08:24,969
[Taiki] <i>Once again,
I don't know where we stand.</i>

158
00:08:25,053 --> 00:08:28,723
Welcome home. Oh, did you
buy something while you were out?

159
00:08:28,806 --> 00:08:30,099
This is...

160
00:08:33,019 --> 00:08:34,187
a secret.

161
00:08:40,944 --> 00:08:42,237
[sighs]

162
00:08:44,447 --> 00:08:46,491
Is this too much? Or too little?

163
00:08:46,574 --> 00:08:48,743
DON'T OVERWATER.
WILL FLOWER WITH SUNLIGHT.

164
00:08:50,912 --> 00:08:52,121
[sighs]

165
00:08:55,291 --> 00:08:56,668
You said it's called "Fall Camp?"

166
00:08:56,751 --> 00:08:57,794
Yup, yup.

167
00:08:57,877 --> 00:08:59,087
It's four whole days.

168
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:01,548
It's always on a long weekend
this time of year.

169
00:09:02,131 --> 00:09:05,009
This year, we're all excited
'cause it's gonna be a joint training camp

170
00:09:05,093 --> 00:09:07,178
with the basketball
and rhythmic gymnastics clubs.

171
00:09:07,262 --> 00:09:09,847
[boy 1] And the lodgings there
are pretty nice, too.

172
00:09:09,931 --> 00:09:12,058
But the practice drills are absolute hell.

173
00:09:12,141 --> 00:09:13,518
[exclaims]

174
00:09:13,601 --> 00:09:14,561
GRIN

175
00:09:14,644 --> 00:09:16,938
Oh! That sounds great.

176
00:09:17,021 --> 00:09:21,025
<i>Everybody staying in one place?
It's gonna be fun!</i>

177
00:09:21,109 --> 00:09:23,945
<i>Since the basketball team
is going to be staying with us...</i>

178
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:29,826
<i>it'll be a chance for Chii and fab-hair
to get to know each other better.</i>

179
00:09:31,077 --> 00:09:32,161
[grunts]

180
00:09:32,704 --> 00:09:33,705
[sighs]

181
00:09:33,788 --> 00:09:36,457
Leave it to me.

182
00:09:37,125 --> 00:09:37,959
[grunts]

183
00:09:38,876 --> 00:09:41,879
{\an8}<i>This is our chance to get
Inota and Hina-bean together!</i>

184
00:09:41,963 --> 00:09:42,839
{\an8}[Hina] Hm?

185
00:09:43,548 --> 00:09:46,801
[Ayame] <i>I mean, if a girl
as cute as Hina-bean confesses to you,</i>

186
00:09:46,884 --> 00:09:49,053
<i>you'd be out of your mind not to date her.</i>

187
00:09:49,137 --> 00:09:50,471
- [shuttlecock thudding]
- Mm?

188
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,390
[grunts]

189
00:09:55,852 --> 00:09:59,272
Is it just me or is Inota
actually good at badminton?

190
00:09:59,355 --> 00:10:01,274
{\an8}He's one of our strongest players.

191
00:10:01,357 --> 00:10:04,402
{\an8}And you wouldn't be wrong
in saying he's the best first-year.

192
00:10:05,111 --> 00:10:07,697
{\an8}I mean, he even beat Yusa the other day.

193
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:11,534
What? Wasn't Yusa wearing
resistance weights on his arms and legs?

194
00:10:11,618 --> 00:10:12,785
That's how he trains.

195
00:10:13,578 --> 00:10:16,164
[Ayame] <i>Hmm. He's better than I expected.</i>

196
00:10:16,247 --> 00:10:19,542
Oh, Miss Manager, could you
grab shuttles from the staff room?

197
00:10:19,626 --> 00:10:21,419
[groans]

198
00:10:21,502 --> 00:10:24,047
[Taiki] <i>Ever since
the practice match against Yusa,</i>

199
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:26,174
<i>I feel like I'm actually getting better.</i>

200
00:10:26,799 --> 00:10:29,844
<i>Even after a second game,
my legs aren't tired.</i>

201
00:10:29,927 --> 00:10:32,180
<i>And I don't lose my balance
on round-the-head shots.</i>

202
00:10:32,805 --> 00:10:34,223
<i>I'm in good shape.</i>

203
00:10:35,266 --> 00:10:36,934
[inaudible]

204
00:10:37,644 --> 00:10:40,146
<i>But he still hasn't played
against me lately.</i>

205
00:10:40,855 --> 00:10:41,939
[Ayame] Inota!

206
00:10:42,023 --> 00:10:44,651
Let's go to the staff room,
and pick up our shuttles.

207
00:10:44,734 --> 00:10:46,569
I'm in the middle of taking a break.

208
00:10:46,653 --> 00:10:49,697
Haven't you heard,
stopping suddenly is bad for you?

209
00:10:49,781 --> 00:10:51,616
Ah, you're thinking of marathons.

210
00:10:51,699 --> 00:10:53,576
Okay, and here we go.

211
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:55,078
[exclaims softly]

212
00:10:56,913 --> 00:10:58,081
[exclaims softly]

213
00:10:58,748 --> 00:11:00,708
[Kazuma] Natsu! Here's your new face!

214
00:11:01,751 --> 00:11:02,835
Matsuoka.

215
00:11:03,628 --> 00:11:05,588
And Chii, spacing out, as usual.

216
00:11:05,671 --> 00:11:07,340
I wasn't spacing out.

217
00:11:07,423 --> 00:11:09,258
{\an8}Oh, no, you totally were.

218
00:11:09,342 --> 00:11:11,844
{\an8}If you'd stayed like that,
you would've turned into a statue

219
00:11:11,928 --> 00:11:15,223
{\an8}and been hailed as Eimei's monument
to the beautiful basketball girl.

220
00:11:15,306 --> 00:11:17,225
{\an8}Where do you come up with this stuff?

221
00:11:18,017 --> 00:11:18,976
[laughs]

222
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:21,062
[mischievous music playing]

223
00:11:21,145 --> 00:11:25,400
[groans] Now that I'm manager,
it's, "Go here," "Do this."

224
00:11:25,483 --> 00:11:27,485
Yeah, and I'm helping you, so ease up.

225
00:11:27,568 --> 00:11:28,903
{\an8}Before I started this gig,

226
00:11:28,986 --> 00:11:31,489
{\an8}I thought all I would be doing
was handing drinks to Yusa.

227
00:11:31,572 --> 00:11:33,616
Oh. Hey, Ayame.

228
00:11:33,699 --> 00:11:34,909
[Ayame] Hi there.

229
00:11:34,992 --> 00:11:37,745
- You really did join a club, then.
- [Ayame] Impressive, right?

230
00:11:37,829 --> 00:11:39,539
I don't think you'll last a week.

231
00:11:39,622 --> 00:11:40,790
Okay, shut up.

232
00:11:40,873 --> 00:11:42,333
Well, hang in there.

233
00:11:48,131 --> 00:11:49,549
- Yo.
- Hey.

234
00:11:52,468 --> 00:11:54,011
Seems like you know everybody.

235
00:11:54,095 --> 00:11:55,388
That's one way to put it.

236
00:11:55,471 --> 00:11:57,765
- They're both my exes.
- Both of them?

237
00:11:58,516 --> 00:12:00,685
{\an8}Yeah, the first guy was summer last year.

238
00:12:00,768 --> 00:12:04,397
{\an8}The second one who said hi to us,
he was beginning of this year, I think.

239
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,400
{\an8}But they both ended on good terms,
so don't freak out.

240
00:12:07,483 --> 00:12:09,652
{\an8}She'd compete at an intergalactic level.

241
00:12:10,236 --> 00:12:12,530
It must be nice to have
such a busy love life.

242
00:12:12,613 --> 00:12:15,408
[sighs internally]
<i>I'll never know what that's like.</i>

243
00:12:15,491 --> 00:12:17,410
It's not a numbers game, Inota.

244
00:12:17,493 --> 00:12:22,415
My methodology is about dating anybody
who tells me they like me.

245
00:12:22,498 --> 00:12:23,749
[exclaims softly]

246
00:12:24,917 --> 00:12:28,963
Of course, I do have to shut down the guys
who aren't remotely my type.

247
00:12:29,046 --> 00:12:31,048
[Taiki] <i>Well, that's just casually rude.</i>

248
00:12:31,132 --> 00:12:33,176
Then where does Yusa fit in?

249
00:12:33,259 --> 00:12:36,929
[Ayame] This has nothing to do with Yusa.
I mean...

250
00:12:37,555 --> 00:12:38,764
To dumb it down for you,

251
00:12:38,848 --> 00:12:41,684
if someone tells me they like me,
I definitely appreciate it.

252
00:12:43,603 --> 00:12:45,313
Because if I don't like them then,

253
00:12:45,396 --> 00:12:47,690
I might come to like them
if the two of us start dating.

254
00:12:48,274 --> 00:12:50,568
And if that's the case,
why wouldn't I give it a try?

255
00:12:51,444 --> 00:12:55,448
Even if there was someone else I liked
between trying to get their attention,

256
00:12:56,032 --> 00:12:59,160
and coming around to somebody
who tells me that they like me,

257
00:12:59,243 --> 00:13:02,079
the second option
seems like it would take less time.

258
00:13:02,163 --> 00:13:03,331
[gasps]

259
00:13:05,041 --> 00:13:08,878
<i>So how about it, Inota?
Give dating Hina-bean a try!</i>

260
00:13:08,961 --> 00:13:09,837
[Taiki] You're right.

261
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:13,090
Getting confessed to
does make you think about them.

262
00:13:13,174 --> 00:13:14,342
[gasps]

263
00:13:14,425 --> 00:13:16,093
Huh? Huh?

264
00:13:16,802 --> 00:13:17,887
We're back, guys.

265
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:21,098
<i>Wait! Hold on!
Does this mean what I think it means?</i>

266
00:13:21,766 --> 00:13:22,850
[exclaims internally]

267
00:13:23,559 --> 00:13:25,603
<i>Things are looking good, Hina-bean!</i>

268
00:13:27,688 --> 00:13:30,608
We're going this year, too, huh?
The fall training camp!

269
00:13:31,234 --> 00:13:32,735
I've heard it's really tough, though.

270
00:13:32,818 --> 00:13:35,530
Yeah, I've heard it starts
with a run in the mountains.

271
00:13:35,613 --> 00:13:37,615
We're gonna be staying
at such a nice place,

272
00:13:37,698 --> 00:13:39,534
but we won't get to enjoy it at all.

273
00:13:39,617 --> 00:13:42,495
And I think the hotel is run by someone
who went to Eimei.

274
00:13:42,578 --> 00:13:43,496
Oh, for real?

275
00:13:43,579 --> 00:13:47,291
That's why it's so cheap to stay,
even though we're such a huge group.

276
00:13:47,375 --> 00:13:51,003
And have you heard this one yet?
The superstition about the campfire?

277
00:13:51,671 --> 00:13:53,130
[Nagisa] Superstition?

278
00:13:53,214 --> 00:13:55,758
So you know how there's always
a campfire on the last night?

279
00:13:56,384 --> 00:13:59,595
<i>The superstition is that,
if someone confesses their love there,</i>

280
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:02,431
{\an8}the fire will ignite in their hearts
and they'll fall for each other.

281
00:14:02,515 --> 00:14:04,016
{\an8}[Nagisa] What a cliche way to say it!

282
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:07,562
Last year, some seniors from badminton
and volleyball started dating.

283
00:14:07,645 --> 00:14:09,021
It could be a coincidence.

284
00:14:09,105 --> 00:14:10,773
It happened the year before, too!

285
00:14:10,856 --> 00:14:13,276
Is there even anyone
you like in the first place?

286
00:14:13,359 --> 00:14:14,277
Uh, what?

287
00:14:20,491 --> 00:14:21,868
[adventurous music playing]

288
00:14:23,077 --> 00:14:25,413
[Ayame] <i>Two hours of a bumpy bus ride.</i>

289
00:14:25,496 --> 00:14:28,082
{\an8}<i>A hotel in the fresh mountain air.</i>

290
00:14:28,165 --> 00:14:31,002
{\an8}<i>Four days and three nights
of non-stop sports.</i>

291
00:14:31,085 --> 00:14:34,672
{\an8}<i>Badminton, basketball,
and gymnastics, all in one place.</i>

292
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:39,176
<i>Let the games begin.</i>

293
00:14:41,262 --> 00:14:42,513
[screams]

294
00:14:42,597 --> 00:14:43,973
A spider!

295
00:14:44,056 --> 00:14:46,058
- [Taiki] <i>This trip may just kill her.</i>
- [Ayame] No!

296
00:14:51,147 --> 00:14:54,066
[Nishida] Don't slow down now!
Keep moving!

297
00:14:54,150 --> 00:14:55,693
{\an8}You got this, guys!

298
00:14:55,776 --> 00:14:59,196
- [girl 2] Push! Come on!
- [pants, grunts]

299
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:00,239
[all grunting]

300
00:15:00,323 --> 00:15:02,700
Don't pick up the pace out of nowhere!

301
00:15:03,284 --> 00:15:06,370
[Coach Yuasa] Keep those legs moving!
Run until the end!

302
00:15:06,454 --> 00:15:07,955
High knees on the way back!

303
00:15:08,456 --> 00:15:09,457
Stay focused.

304
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,542
Last one! And now a burpee!

305
00:15:11,626 --> 00:15:12,710
[adventurous music ends]

306
00:15:12,793 --> 00:15:14,503
[whistle blows]

307
00:15:14,587 --> 00:15:16,088
All right! Take a break.

308
00:15:16,172 --> 00:15:18,090
[all panting, groaning]

309
00:15:20,676 --> 00:15:22,720
Next up, we've got some footwork drills.

310
00:15:22,803 --> 00:15:23,971
I'm dying.

311
00:15:24,055 --> 00:15:25,973
We've done legs the entire morning.

312
00:15:26,057 --> 00:15:28,476
And we have
a walling hell fest in the afternoon.

313
00:15:28,559 --> 00:15:31,646
[boy] How is it that we drove
two whole hours to get here,

314
00:15:31,729 --> 00:15:34,273
and yet we're looking at the same scenery?

315
00:15:34,357 --> 00:15:35,983
Taiki, open the door.

316
00:15:36,067 --> 00:15:38,152
We need to air this place out.

317
00:15:38,235 --> 00:15:39,612
[Taiki] Yeah.

318
00:15:40,279 --> 00:15:41,739
[boy] Basketball is running?

319
00:15:41,822 --> 00:15:43,866
But they just ran with us
in the mountains!

320
00:15:44,450 --> 00:15:46,202
Their gym is a bit further away,

321
00:15:46,285 --> 00:15:49,622
{\an8}so I guess they get the bonus
of having to run all the way there.

322
00:15:49,705 --> 00:15:50,748
{\an8}That sucks.

323
00:15:50,831 --> 00:15:52,249
[Taiki gasps]

324
00:15:58,631 --> 00:16:01,509
[boy] Why does rhythmic gymnastics
get to ride around in a bus?

325
00:16:01,592 --> 00:16:04,261
{\an8}It's 'cause our gym
is too far away! Ta-ta!

326
00:16:04,345 --> 00:16:05,721
[boy] That's no fair!

327
00:16:05,805 --> 00:16:07,014
[girl laughs]

328
00:16:07,723 --> 00:16:10,267
It's a good thing our gym's
connected to the main building.

329
00:16:10,351 --> 00:16:11,811
[boy] Hard pass on running.

330
00:16:11,894 --> 00:16:12,895
Hey,

331
00:16:13,729 --> 00:16:15,147
break's almost over!

332
00:16:15,231 --> 00:16:17,733
Could you secretly make it
a little longer?

333
00:16:17,817 --> 00:16:19,652
[Ayame] You obviously know
I can't do that.

334
00:16:19,735 --> 00:16:22,154
Please have mercy on us, Manager!

335
00:16:22,238 --> 00:16:24,115
[shuttlecock thudding]

336
00:16:26,659 --> 00:16:27,827
[grunts]

337
00:16:29,245 --> 00:16:30,746
[energetic music playing]

338
00:16:32,081 --> 00:16:34,250
[indistinct chatter]

339
00:16:35,418 --> 00:16:36,752
[munching aggressively]

340
00:16:37,461 --> 00:16:38,838
Tea, anyone? Tea?

341
00:16:38,921 --> 00:16:41,090
[shuttlecock thudding]

342
00:16:42,675 --> 00:16:43,759
[grunts]

343
00:16:45,177 --> 00:16:46,929
[energetic music ends]

344
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:51,100
- [thudding]
- [all panting]

345
00:16:52,476 --> 00:16:54,103
TOTAL ANNIHILATION

346
00:16:57,606 --> 00:16:59,108
- [Taiki] Haryu.
- Mm?

347
00:16:59,734 --> 00:17:01,610
Wanna play a practice match with me?

348
00:17:02,194 --> 00:17:04,613
I want to take stock of
what I need to work on.

349
00:17:05,698 --> 00:17:08,868
- No.
<i>- No? What is he, a child?</i>

350
00:17:09,785 --> 00:17:12,371
<i>Haryu's the strongest player on the team,</i>

351
00:17:12,455 --> 00:17:15,332
<i>so I want to go up against him
as much as I can.</i>

352
00:17:16,042 --> 00:17:18,127
[boy] Taiki, let's practice our shots!

353
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:19,378
Coming!

354
00:17:22,298 --> 00:17:23,632
[Nishida] Good gracious!

355
00:17:23,716 --> 00:17:26,135
The best bath in years.

356
00:17:26,218 --> 00:17:28,763
Why are you talking
like an old man, Nishida?

357
00:17:28,846 --> 00:17:30,890
He is right, though, it was a nice bath.

358
00:17:30,973 --> 00:17:32,183
Listen, fellas.

359
00:17:32,725 --> 00:17:34,477
The key to being a gentleman

360
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:37,521
is that, even if you think of girls
after a bath, you keep quiet.

361
00:17:37,605 --> 00:17:39,398
You're not keeping quiet, are you?

362
00:17:40,024 --> 00:17:41,275
<i>I guess this means...</i>

363
00:17:42,234 --> 00:17:45,196
<i>that other people
are going to see how Chinatsu looks</i>

364
00:17:45,279 --> 00:17:47,281
<i>straight out of the bath, too.</i>

365
00:17:48,074 --> 00:17:50,659
[groans] <i>That's been my secret privilege!</i>

366
00:17:51,452 --> 00:17:53,037
[Hina] Well, you look worn out.

367
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,663
[funky music playing]

368
00:17:56,123 --> 00:17:57,291
Hina.

369
00:17:57,917 --> 00:18:00,211
- I'll go on and head back.
- [Hina] Yeah.

370
00:18:00,878 --> 00:18:02,630
You're wearing your hair down.

371
00:18:02,713 --> 00:18:04,673
Yeah, it's 'cause I just blow-dried it.

372
00:18:06,133 --> 00:18:07,301
Anyway, what's up?

373
00:18:07,384 --> 00:18:09,804
It feels like forever since I've seen you.

374
00:18:12,890 --> 00:18:15,309
Well, gosh, this has
really been a long day.

375
00:18:15,392 --> 00:18:18,312
I'm beat, so I'll just go to bed
to be ready for tomorrow--

376
00:18:18,395 --> 00:18:21,565
What are you saying?
The night has only just begun!

377
00:18:21,649 --> 00:18:24,443
We're staying at a hotel.
Don't you wanna have some fun?

378
00:18:24,527 --> 00:18:27,822
We gotta live it up!
And that's why I brought a game with me!

379
00:18:27,905 --> 00:18:30,449
A game? I wanna play, too.

380
00:18:31,117 --> 00:18:31,951
O-ho!

381
00:18:32,034 --> 00:18:34,954
And you two there.
You're coming with us, too.

382
00:18:37,039 --> 00:18:39,458
Why does this have to take place
in my room?

383
00:18:39,542 --> 00:18:41,293
[Nishida] It's our room actually!

384
00:18:43,170 --> 00:18:44,964
So, what're we playing?

385
00:18:45,047 --> 00:18:47,758
[chuckles] Well, buckle up,
my dear friends.

386
00:18:48,425 --> 00:18:50,719
{\an8}It's called the King's Card Game!

387
00:18:50,803 --> 00:18:53,222
{\an8}- Nope, sounds lame.
- [Nagisa] Maybe we head out.

388
00:18:53,305 --> 00:18:54,223
{\an8}Hold up, hold up!

389
00:18:54,306 --> 00:18:57,977
This game is way more fun
than you're giving it credit for. Come on.

390
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:01,355
So check this out. We have
these cards that act as the "king."

391
00:19:01,438 --> 00:19:03,190
First, we all draw cards,

392
00:19:03,274 --> 00:19:06,235
and whoever gets the servant card
becomes the one to get a decree.

393
00:19:06,318 --> 00:19:09,488
{\an8}Then, you draw a "royal decree" card,
and you have to do whatever it says.

394
00:19:09,572 --> 00:19:10,614
{\an8}GET FLICKED IN THE HEAD

395
00:19:12,241 --> 00:19:13,617
[groans]

396
00:19:14,952 --> 00:19:17,496
You know, this game
is starting to grow on me.

397
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:19,248
[groaning]

398
00:19:20,082 --> 00:19:22,084
- I think we should give it a try.
- [Nishida laughs]

399
00:19:22,168 --> 00:19:24,003
So everyone should take a card now.

400
00:19:25,212 --> 00:19:26,422
[Kyo] Mm?

401
00:19:26,505 --> 00:19:27,423
Kyo got it.

402
00:19:27,506 --> 00:19:29,133
Then you draw your royal decree.

403
00:19:31,218 --> 00:19:32,887
{\an8}END EVERY SENTENCE WITH "MEOW"

404
00:19:36,724 --> 00:19:37,892
Is this right, meow?

405
00:19:37,975 --> 00:19:40,978
You're just gonna do what it says?
No questions asked?

406
00:19:41,061 --> 00:19:43,522
[Kyo] In these games, you lose
if you get embarrassed, meow.

407
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,900
[Nishida] Next round, next round.

408
00:19:46,859 --> 00:19:47,776
Who's the servant?

409
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:49,236
[Nagisa] Oh, it's Chinatsu!

410
00:19:50,613 --> 00:19:53,032
[Taiki] <i>Show me meow card!
Come on, meow card!</i>

411
00:19:54,867 --> 00:19:57,036
{\an8}412
I have to get my hair done?

412
00:19:57,119 --> 00:20:00,456
Oh, I've got this.
I have plenty of hair ties and stuff.

413
00:20:00,539 --> 00:20:02,708
{\an8}I've got a bunch
of hair stuff with me, too.

414
00:20:02,791 --> 00:20:05,419
I'm gonna give you
the most incredible updo.

415
00:20:05,502 --> 00:20:07,963
Prepare thyself, young Chinatsu.

416
00:20:08,047 --> 00:20:09,173
[Chinatsu exclaims]

417
00:20:09,256 --> 00:20:11,300
Wait! Oh, no, that's too...

418
00:20:11,383 --> 00:20:13,802
[Nagisa] You!
Keep your hands on your knees!

419
00:20:17,139 --> 00:20:18,057
[all chuckle]

420
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,808
[all laughing]

421
00:20:19,892 --> 00:20:21,185
[Ayame] It's so adorable!

422
00:20:21,268 --> 00:20:22,937
This is absolute gold.

423
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:24,188
Sending to Karen.

424
00:20:24,271 --> 00:20:25,940
Nice job with the hair ties.

425
00:20:26,023 --> 00:20:28,609
[Chinatsu] It's too embarrassing
if it's only me.

426
00:20:29,401 --> 00:20:31,445
[laughing]

427
00:20:32,529 --> 00:20:34,823
{\an8}[Haryu] You can't let your guard down
playing this game.

428
00:20:34,907 --> 00:20:36,825
{\an8}I think watching is more fun than playing.

429
00:20:36,909 --> 00:20:40,204
[Ayame] <i>It would seem
that no one has noticed yet.</i>

430
00:20:40,829 --> 00:20:43,958
<i>This game has a foolproof way to win!</i>

431
00:20:44,041 --> 00:20:46,210
<i>There! The servant card...</i>

432
00:20:46,293 --> 00:20:48,712
<i>is slightly dented on one side.</i>

433
00:20:49,380 --> 00:20:53,717
<i>By taking notice of that small detail,
I'll be able to dominate this game.</i>

434
00:20:53,801 --> 00:20:55,803
Okie-dokie! I'll deal next round!

435
00:20:55,886 --> 00:20:57,763
Yours. There.

436
00:20:58,430 --> 00:20:59,515
For you.

437
00:21:00,182 --> 00:21:01,725
And for you.

438
00:21:01,809 --> 00:21:03,018
There.

439
00:21:03,102 --> 00:21:04,270
And yours.

440
00:21:06,105 --> 00:21:07,106
I got it.

441
00:21:07,189 --> 00:21:08,607
[Ayame] <i>Just as I planned.</i>

442
00:21:08,691 --> 00:21:09,692
STARE

443
00:21:09,775 --> 00:21:13,153
<i>During the last turn, I happened to catch
a glimpse of what the next card is.</i>

444
00:21:13,237 --> 00:21:14,863
STARE AT THE PERSON TO YOUR LEFT

445
00:21:14,947 --> 00:21:17,366
<i>And I thought, "This royal decree
has Inota's name on it!"</i>

446
00:21:17,449 --> 00:21:21,745
<i>If he locks eyes with Hina-bean,
Inota will completely fall for her.</i>

447
00:21:21,829 --> 00:21:23,330
How bout I shuffle the cards?

448
00:21:24,039 --> 00:21:27,126
{\an8}- No! [groans]
- Sir, Taiki, here's your card.

449
00:21:27,209 --> 00:21:28,544
{\an8}Thanks, Nishida.

450
00:21:29,336 --> 00:21:31,297
{\an8}DECLARE YOUR LOVE TO YOUR LOVED ONE!

451
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,381
[gasps]

452
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:35,509
Oh, that's a great card!

453
00:21:35,592 --> 00:21:38,137
This is starting to feel
like a slumber party!

454
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:39,513
[Taiki] Like my parents?

455
00:21:39,596 --> 00:21:41,765
No, you fool, like someone you like-like.

456
00:21:41,849 --> 00:21:44,393
And everybody here will keep your secret!

457
00:21:44,476 --> 00:21:45,811
So! Out with it!

458
00:21:46,729 --> 00:21:48,022
[mellow music playing]

459
00:21:48,105 --> 00:21:49,398
[Taiki sighs]

460
00:21:58,866 --> 00:22:02,286
[Taiki] <i>The person I like is...</i>

461
00:22:05,539 --> 00:22:07,541
[closing theme song playing]
